  <b>Nothing here is executed.</b> No table is renamed, no migration is written, no caller is swept.
  The §R8 precedent sets the bar: renaming <em>four</em> tables is already owner-gated, scoped at 312
  tracked files, and forbidden to attempt piecemeal. This covers <em>sixty-six</em>. It exists so the
  rename can be ruled on once, as a grammar, instead of table by table forever.
</div>

