  <h3>B.2 — Nothing points into judgment, and nothing points into render</h3>
  <p>Zero cross-stage foreign keys target a judgment or render table.
  <span class="m">specifications.specification_id</span> is referenced by exactly one thing —
  <span class="m">specification_source_links</span>, in its own stage.</p>
  <p>That is <em>correct</em> under rule 5: later stages reach back, earlier stages do not reach
  forward. Three exceptions run the other way, and each is a promotion edge someone will eventually
  want to delete as redundant.</p>
  <div class="scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Pointer</th><th>Direction</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m">citation_mining.global_ref_id</span></td><td class="sub">research → evidence</td><td>a mined lead that got admitted</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m">source_value_extractions.promoted_to_rdc_id</span></td><td class="sub">evidence → synthesis</td><td>an extraction that became a cited claim</td></tr>
      <tr class="fault"><td><span class="m">item_population_elaborations.evidence_ref_id</span></td><td class="sub"><b>substrate → evidence</b></td><td>substrate citing a stage, which inverts the model</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h3>B.3 — The <span class="m">REF-</span> namespace is two tables sharing one id space with no key between them</h3>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="panel">
      <h4>The split</h4>
      <div class="scroll" style="margin:0;border:none;background:none"><table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><span class="m">source_locators</span> <span class="chip st-research">research</span></td><td class="num">875</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="m">evidence_sources</span> <span class="chip st-evidence">evidence</span></td><td class="num">10</td></tr>
          <tr><td>present in <b>both</b></td><td class="num">4</td></tr>
          <tr><td>only in the clue store</td><td class="num">871</td></tr>
          <tr class="fault"><td>admitted, <b>no clue-store row</b></td><td class="num">6</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h4>Eleven ids do not match the format</h4>
      <p class="note"><span class="m">source_locators</span> holds
      <span class="m">REF-VERIFIED-001</span> … <span class="m">-012</span>, which sort
      <em>above</em> every numbered id. So <span class="m">MAX(ref_id)</span> returns
      <span class="m">REF-VERIFIED-012</span>, not <span class="m">REF-00964</span> — any
      hand-rolled high-water mark is wrong today.
      <span class="m">dbcore.next_ref_id()</span> is the sanctioned computation.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>There is <b>no foreign key in either direction</b>, and the id space is shared — so
  <span class="m">REF-00325</span> does not tell you which stage it lives in.</p>

  <h3>B.4 — Seven column names for one referent, three of them lying</h3>
  <div class="scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Column</th><th class="num">Non-null</th><th>Keyed</th><th>What it actually holds</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m">evidence_sources.ref_id</span></td><td class="num">10</td><td class="sub">is the target</td><td><span class="m">REF-00325</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m">citation_mining.global_ref_id</span></td><td class="num">10</td><td>yes</td><td>a ref_id</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m">reasoning_doc_citations.source_ref_id</span></td><td class="num">0</td><td>yes</td><td>a ref_id</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m">source_value_extractions.root_ref_id</span></td><td class="num">0</td><td>yes</td><td>a ref_id</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m">item_population_elaborations.evidence_ref_id</span></td><td class="num">0</td><td>yes</td><td>a ref_id</td></tr>
      <tr class="fault"><td><span class="m">evidence_sources.superseded_by_ref_id</span></td><td class="num">0</td><td><b>no</b></td><td>a ref_id, unenforced</td></tr>
